# tests/recursion/slotfamilies.rxt -- module `recursion` ([DD-14]): SS5.3b: the two MEASURED slot families a naive `W` loses -- PENDING (a lost match) and CUT_MARK (a false match)
#
# GENERATED BY tests/recursion/gen_corpus.py, and that is a property rather
# than a convenience: every expectation below -- including every `g` line --
# was produced by driving the cell through libpcre2 10.46 (via the committed
# ctypes binding at docs/design/subroutines_measurements/probes/sr_oracle.py,
# which borrows la_oracle.py -> br_oracle.py -> pcre2_ctypes.py) BEFORE it was
# written. The generator never asks pcrec anything.
#
# THE SOLE ORACLE IS LIBPCRE2 -- THERE IS NO PYTHON ARM, AND THAT IS AN
# ABSENCE RATHER THAN A DIVERGENCE (design SS10.1). python3 `re` has no
# subroutine-call construct at all: every one of the nine call spellings plus
# both zero spellings raises `re.error` at compile time. `\\1` and `(?P=n)`
# DO compile in python, but they are `backrefs`' reference construct, not this
# module's call construct (design SS2.1's one-cell discriminator is why
# `spellings.rxt` opens with it) -- so marking this corpus python-verifiable
# on the strength of those two spellings would be checking the wrong module.
#
# `(?(DEFINE)...)` IS THIS MODULE'S SINCE [DD-14] WAVE F (D71 item 4,
# overruling design SS2.5's "RULED: no DEFINE"). It is a TAILED row on the
# `(?(` doorway -- the rest of `(?(` is still `conditionals`' -- and it lowers
# to the SAME NODE the `{0}`-callee idiom produces, an A_REP with
# rmin == rmax == 0 over the body. That is why define.rxt and zerodef.rxt
# carry the two spellings SIDE BY SIDE on the same cells: they are two
# spellings of one construct, and the corpus asserts they agree rather than
# assuming it. Where a body must be callee-only, `{0}` remains the spelling
# used in the OTHER files, because those cells were oracle-verified in that
# form and re-spelling them would move a measurement without re-measuring it.
#
# NOTHING IN src/ IMPLEMENTS A SUBROUTINE CALL YET. Every ordinary `m`/`n`
# block in this corpus is therefore EXPECTED to report a pattern-compile
# failure under today's harness (`requires module 'recursion'`) -- that is
# the correct, documented state before [DD-14] wave B+C lands (docs/
# testing.md's "expected-unsupported" policy), not a corpus defect.
#
# Design: docs/design/subroutines_design.md. Decisions: docs/dev/decisions.md
# D71 (the give-up-code axis, D71.1) and D72 (PCREC_ERR_INTERNAL).

# ====================================================================
# AXIS P -- SLOT_GROUP<n>_PENDING (design SS5.3b): a backreference MARKS the called group, so publish-at-close needs a pending slot; without it the inner activation's open position clobbers the outer's and the outer LOSES ITS MATCH.
# ====================================================================

# MEASURED 11/2 disagree without the pending slot (design SS5.3b); WITH it, 13/0.
pattern ^(a(?1)?b)\1$
features recursion,backrefs
m "aabbaabb" 0 8
g 1 0 4
m "aaabbbaaabbb" 0 12
g 1 0 6

# ====================================================================
# AXIS C -- SLOT_CUT_MARK<n> (design SS5.3b): an atomic group LIVE AT TWO DEPTHS needs one mark instance per emitted copy; without it the inner activation's mark clobbers the outer's `RX_CUT` into a no-op and the atomic group stops being atomic -- a FALSE MATCH, and the false-match set is EXACTLY the non-atomic control's language.
# ====================================================================

# 10.46 matches NOTHING at any of these lengths -- MEASURED 4/6 disagree without the mark-per-activation family (design SS5.3b).
pattern ^((?>a(?1)?))a$
features recursion,atomic-groups
n "aa"
n "aaa"
n "aaaa"
n "aaaaa"
n "aaaaaa"
n "aaaaaaa"
n "aaaaaaaa"

# THE NON-ATOMIC CONTROL -- the exact language the false matches above would reproduce on a broken compiler.
pattern ^((?:a(?1)?))a$
features recursion
m "aa" 0 2
g 1 0 1
m "aaa" 0 3
g 1 0 2

# ====================================================================
# THE THREE ARGUED FAMILIES, ONE CELL EACH (design SS5.3b's five ARGUED rows, collapsed to the three that a pattern can reach). SS5.3b measured TWO families (PENDING and CUT_MARK) and REASONED about five; each cell below is a callee that ALLOCATES the family in question and is RE-ENTERED at two depths, which is the configuration the argument is about -- a slot written at a construct's ENTRY and read at its EXIT, with two ACTIVATIONS of one emitted copy NESTED rather than sequential. Each was checked to allocate its family in the shipped artifact before being written: the slot legend names it.
# ====================================================================

# SLOT_EMPTY_GUARD (S-SR6c) and SLOT_SPAN_LOW (S-SR6d). The callee holds `(?:a?)*` -- an UNBOUNDED frames-rung quantifier with a NULLABLE body, which is the ONLY shape that allocates an empty guard: MEASURED, `^(a?){0,5}$` allocates NONE while `^(a?)*$` and `^(a?)+$` allocate one each, so a bounded cell would go green on a broken compiler. Artifact legend: RX_SLOT_EMPTY_GUARD0 and RX_SLOT_SPAN_LOW0.
pattern ^(?:(?<g>(?:a?)*b(?&g)?)){0}(?&g)$
features recursion,named-groups
m "b" 0 1
g 1 -1 -1
m "bb" 0 2
g 1 -1 -1
m "ab" 0 2
g 1 -1 -1
m "abb" 0 3
g 1 -1 -1
m "aabb" 0 4
g 1 -1 -1
m "abab" 0 4
g 1 -1 -1
n ""

# SLOT_SPAN_LOW (S-SR6d) on its own, without the guard: `a{1,3}` takes the CURSOR rung and allocates a low-water mark. WHICH RUNG a body gets is a compile-time choice the design says this cell has to be written against as LANDED rather than as predicted; the artifact legend is what was read (RX_SLOT_SPAN_LOW0, no guard).
pattern ^(?:(?<g>a{1,3}b(?&g)?)){0}(?&g)$
features recursion,named-groups
m "ab" 0 2
g 1 -1 -1
m "aab" 0 3
g 1 -1 -1
m "abab" 0 4
g 1 -1 -1
m "aabaab" 0 6
g 1 -1 -1
m "aaab" 0 4
g 1 -1 -1
n "a"

# SLOT_LOOK_MARK and SLOT_LOOK_POS (S-SR6e), the family SS5.3b could not measure because [M6.6.2] had not landed -- and the family SS12 P-2's FIRST version predicted was SAFE "because each is re-initialised at its own entry label on every entry". That prediction is WITHDRAWN: the re-initialisation is not the question, the OVERWRITE is. A lookahead INSIDE a recursive callee is live at two depths. Artifact legend: RX_SLOT_LOOK_MARK0 and RX_SLOT_LOOK_POS0.
pattern ^(?:(?<g>(?=a)a(?&g)?b)){0}(?&g)$
features recursion,lookaround,named-groups
m "ab" 0 2
g 1 -1 -1
m "aabb" 0 4
g 1 -1 -1
m "aaabbb" 0 6
g 1 -1 -1
n "a"
n "abb"
